  "title": "",
  "body": "  Q-4: What will happen if you try to open a file that does not exist?      the program will close    If a file does not exist, the program will not close, but cannot run as expected.      nothing    Something *will* happen if the file does not exist.      open will fail    If a file does not exist, open will fail and you will get an error.      the program will create a new file    The program will not make a new file on its own if it tries to open a file that does not exist.     "
