  "body": "  What is the name of the following function?   def drawSquare(t, sz): \"\"\"Make turtle t draw a square of with side sz.\"\"\" for i in range(4): t.forward(sz) t.left(90)       def drawSquare(t, sz)   This line is the complete function header (except for the semi-colon) which includes the name as well as several other components.     drawSquare   Yes, the name of the function is given after the keyword def and before the list of parameters.     drawSquare(t, sz)   This includes the function name and its parameters     Make turtle t draw a square with side sz.   This is a comment stating what the function does.    "
