  "url": "functions_functions.html#test_question5_1_5",
  "type": "Checkpoint",
  "number": "4.1.8",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  What are the parameters of the following function?   def drawSquare(t, sz): \"\"\"Make turtle t draw a square of with side sz.\"\"\" for i in range(4): t.forward(sz) t.left(90)       i   i is a variable used inside of the function, but not a parameter, which is passed in to the function.     t   t is only one of the parameters to this function.     t, sz   Yes, the function specifies two parameters: t and sz.     t, sz, i   the parameters include only those variables whose values that the function expects to receive as input. They are specified in the header of the function.    "
