  "number": "5.3.1.1",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  Q-3: Suppose you are doing a sequential search of the list [15, 18, 2, 19, 18, 0, 8, 14, 19, 14]. How many comparisons would you need to do in order to find the key 18?      5    Five comparisons would get the second 18 in the list.      10    You do not need to search the entire list, only until you find the key you are looking for.      4    No, remember in a sequential search you start at the beginning and check each key until you find what you are looking for or exhaust the list.      2    In this case only 2 comparisons were needed to find the key.     "
