  "body": "  Q-4: Suppose you have the following sorted list [3, 5, 6, 8, 11, 12, 14, 15, 17, 18] and are using the recursive binary search algorithm. Which group of numbers correctly shows the sequence of comparisons used to search for the key 16?      11, 14, 17    Looks like you might be guilty of an off-by-one error. Remember the first position is index 0.      18, 17, 15    Remember binary search starts in the middle and halves the list.      14, 17, 15    Looks like you might be off by one, be careful that you are calculating the midpont using integer arithmetic.      12, 17, 15    Binary search starts at the midpoint and halves the list each time. It is done when the list is empty.     "
