  "body": "  What is printed by the following statements?   s = \"We are learning!\" x = 0 for i in s: if i in ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd', 'e']: x += 1 print(x)       2    Though only two of the letters in the list are found, we count them each time they appear.      5    Yes, we add to x each time we come across a letter in the list.      0    Check again what the conditional is evaluating. The value of i will be a character in the string s, so what will happen in the if statement?      There is an error in the code so it cannot run.    There are no errors in this code.     "
