  "body": "  Create a function called distance which returns the distance between two coordinates using the distance formula: d = √((x_2 - x_1)² + (y_2 - y_1)²). Use two functions in Python's math module ( math.pow , math.sqrt ). The function math.pow(a,b) returns a raised to the b power. The function math.sqrt(a) returns the square root of a .     import math     def distance(x1, y1, x2, y2):    def distance(x1, y1, x2, y2)     dx = x2 - x1  dy = y2 - y1     dsquared = math.pow(dx, 2) + math.pow(dy, 2)    dsquared = math.pow(2, dx) + math.pow(2, dy)      result = math.sqrt(dsquared)    result = math.square_root(dsquared)     return result    "
