  "body": "  Create a function called sum_of_split_num that takes in str_num_with_hyphens as a parameter and returns the sum of the integers that are split up by hyphens. For example, sum_of_split_num('978-876-4908') should return 6762 because 978 + 876 + 4908 = 6762. (Note: Integers are 0 or greater.)     def sum_of_split_num(str_num_with_hyphens):     num_without_hyphens = str_num_with_hyphens.split('-')    num_without_hyphens = str_num_with_hyphens.split()     map_object_to_ints = map(int, num_without_hyphens)    lst_of_ints = list(map_object_to_ints)     return sum(lst_of_ints)    return sum(lst_of_ints) \/ 2     return lst_of_ints.sum()    "
